From 7a78caf48c32ceb917f821e21cff3df6f7138c0a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Siomkin Alexander <siomkin.alexander@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 2 Jul 2026 19:24:55 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] GL-100 feat(review): Code/Preview toggle renders markdown
 files
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The single-file review header gets an icon switcher for .md/.markdown
files: Code shows the existing raw diff, Preview renders the file's NEW
side (worktree copy for unstaged, index blob for staged, the commit's
blob otherwise) through the same sanitized GFM pipeline as PR
descriptions (react-markdown + remark-gfm + rehype-sanitize via
components/ui/Markdown) — no new JS dependency. The Unified/Split
toggle hides while previewing, mirroring the binary-card behavior.

Content comes through the existing read_binary_blob command: diffs_to_files
now populates oldOid/newOid for text deltas too (sizes stay binary-only).
The working-tree side of an unstaged diff is deliberately read from disk
by path — libgit2 reports that side with a computed hash that need not
exist in the ODB. Preview is capped at 2 MiB, with deleted/empty/too-large
states in the pane.

Validation: cargo test (207, incl. a new text-oid round-trip test),
bunx tsc --noEmit, bun run test (838, incl. new render tests for the
toggle and the unstaged by-path read), eslint on touched files.
