From 00b13d71ceda75df5b0014d7a0b2b80a75284dd8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Siomkin Alexander <siomkin.alexander@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 3 Jul 2026 11:02:55 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] GL-100 fix(review): selection diffs carry blob oids so
 markdown Preview loads
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Code review caught that the multi-commit selection path (selection_diff_file)
still returned text FileDiffs without oldOid/newOid — only diffs_to_files was
updated in the feature commit. Opening a .md file from a multi-commit
selection and hitting Preview therefore resolved no source and showed "No
content to preview" even though the Code diff rendered fine.

The non-gapped text branch of selection.rs file_diff now carries both blob
oids, mirroring its binary branch and diffs_to_files (sizes stay binary-only).
The gapped composed path (text_diff) intentionally stays oid-less: the merged
result exists only in memory and matches no repo blob, so Preview falls back
to its empty state rather than fetch a blob that would include the unselected
edit — documented on text_diff and in previewSource's doc comment.

Validation: cargo test (210, incl. a new selection oid round-trip test that
also pins the composed-path behavior), bunx tsc --noEmit, bun run test (858).
